diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d7aa67f..0f6faea 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,8 +9,13 @@ Paste a chat or open a WhatsApp (including ZIP), Telegram, Messenger, Instagram,
 Discord, Slack, Teams, iMessage, IRC, LINE, KakaoTalk, CSV or plain transcript.
 Existing import parsers remain in place. With a recognised format the browser
 requires exactly two recognised speakers with at least three text messages each.
-A 40-message, completely fictional sample chat is built in; it includes
-different message lengths and reply gaps, and fits in a single Jev request.
+A 400-message, completely fictional sample chat is built in. Its two fictional
+speakers talk across January–September 2026 about everyday plans, classes,
+support, a clarified misunderstanding and ambiguous friendly jokes. Messages
+use unambiguous day-first dates, varied lengths, gaps and quiet days; the
+sample currently fits within the Jev state budget. The local preview intercepts
+the Jev call and needs no API key. Forecasts are calculated independently:
+never treat the sample as evidence that a real relationship can be predicted.
 A three-person chat cannot be made eligible by hiding or excluding one person.
 A long chat can be truncated to the newest messages that fit Jev's state
 limit; if that excerpt has fewer than three messages from either speaker, no
@@ -130,17 +135,32 @@ prefers reduced motion. Editing the chat while a result or request is visible
 clears the old result; a response for that superseded text is not displayed.
 No extra request, storage, or chat metadata is introduced by this styling.
 
-Each person gets a **visual animal sticker for a counted pattern**, using only
-the part of a parsed chat submitted to Jev. Both need at least three text
-messages; otherwise both receive a neutral sticker. In this order: a **dog**
-starts strictly more of at least three observed conversations than the other
-person (ties get no starter sticker); a **hedgehog** has a median of at least
-15 words per message; a **mouse** has a median of at most 6; everyone else
-gets a **cat**. The numeric observation and `n` (or starts out of conversations)
-appear beside the sticker. Animals represent message patterns, never identities
-or personality. Raw formats get neutral stickers because their speakers cannot
-be verified. For truncated chats the sticker uses only the submitted excerpt;
-the separate existing local statistics can describe the full parsed chat.
+Each person gets one of seven **original animal stickers for a counted pattern**,
+using only the part of a parsed chat submitted to Jev. Both people need at least
+three text messages, otherwise both receive a neutral sticker. Rules run in
+this order (the first qualifying rule wins): **dog** starts strictly more of at
+least three observed conversations than the other person (ties receive no dog);
+**owl** writes at least 5 of 10 timestamped messages between 22:00 and 05:59
+*as written in the export* (no timezone is assumed); **rabbit** has at least
+five valid reply blocks with median response time at most three minutes;
+**tortoise** has at least five valid reply blocks with median response time at
+least 30 minutes; **hedgehog** has median text length at least 15 words over at
+least three messages; **mouse** has median length at most six words over at least
+three messages; otherwise **cat** represents a median between seven and fourteen
+words. A six-hour pause begins a new conversation and is excluded from reply
+gaps. Each sticker displays the observation and sample size. Two people may
+receive the same animal. The rules describe chat roles, never personalities.
+Raw formats get neutral stickers because speakers cannot be verified. For
+truncated chats the sticker uses only the submitted excerpt; separate local
+statistics and the time graph use the whole recognised chat. Result and share
+card explicitly state the two scopes.
+
+The analysis button optionally plays one quiet, locally synthesized two-note
+cue (Web Audio API); the nearby button mutes it without saving a preference.
+The loading animation shows an open-ended active state, not a percentage or
+timed result. Its text stages follow the actual request and local calculations.
+Reduced-motion settings disable its moving elements. A fast request is shown
+immediately, without a minimum animation delay.
 
 The shared duo story uses only the four existing ordinal scores, in order:
 tension >= 2 gives a friction story; otherwise clarity <= 1 gives a clarifying
diff --git a/css/polish.css b/css/polish.css
index 28f8b31..d61705a 100644
--- a/css/polish.css
+++ b/css/polish.css
@@ -62,6 +62,8 @@ body, main, .masthead, .colophon { min-width: 0; }
 .chip { padding: .35rem .8rem; border-color: #bde9ff75; background: #bde9ff1c; font-weight: 700; }
 .intake-bar { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
 .intake-bar .primary { box-shadow: 0 5px 0 #708039; }
+.intake-bar .sound-toggle { min-width: 6.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--rule); color: var(--ink); }
+.sound-toggle[aria-pressed="false"] { color: var(--ink-soft); background: #ffffff0d; }
 .intake-bar .primary:hover:not(:disabled) { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 7px 0 #708039, 0 11px 25px #dff86f33; }
 .intake-bar .primary:active:not(:disabled) { transform: translateY(3px); box-shadow: 0 2px 0 #708039; }
 .primary, .secondary { transition: background .18s ease, box-shadow .18s ease, transform .18s ease; }
@@ -73,6 +75,10 @@ body, main, .masthead, .colophon { min-width: 0; }
 .lab-orbit { position: absolute; inset: 4%; border: 2px dashed var(--accent-blue); border-radius: 50%; animation: orbit 10s linear infinite; }
 .lab-orbit-two { inset: 18%; border-color: var(--accent); animation-direction: reverse; animation-duration: 7s; }
 .lab-symbol { z-index: 1; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 46%; aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 1rem; background: var(--accent); color: #242138; font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem); box-shadow: 0 0 35px #dff86f73; animation: lab-pulse 1.5s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
+.lab-bubble { position: absolute; z-index: 1; width: 28%; height: 19%; border-radius: 60% 60% 60% 18%; background: var(--accent-blue); box-shadow: 0 5px 15px #1119; animation: bubble-travel 1.5s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
+.lab-bubble-a { left: 0; top: 8%; transform: rotate(-12deg); }
+.lab-bubble-b { right: 0; bottom: 8%; transform: rotate(166deg); background: var(--accent-coral); animation-delay: -.75s; }
+@keyframes bubble-travel { to { translate: 12px 10px; opacity: .7; } }
 @keyframes orbit { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
 @keyframes lab-pulse { to { transform: scale(1.08); box-shadow: 0 0 50px #dff86fa8; } }
 .lab-copy { min-width: 0; }
@@ -92,6 +98,7 @@ body, main, .masthead, .colophon { min-width: 0; }
 
 .results { margin-top: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
 .results > .step-label { font-size: .84rem; }
+.scope-note { display: inline-block; margin: .4rem 0 1rem; padding: .65rem 1rem; border: 1px solid #bde9ff75; border-radius: .85rem; background: #bde9ff13; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .9rem; }
 .connection-summary { background: radial-gradient(28rem 28rem at 100% 0%, #6673a055, transparent 80%), linear-gradient(145deg, #402d51, #2c243b 60%, #213744); border-color: #ab93b669; }
 .connection-summary::before { border-color: #ffffff3d; }
 .vibe-hero { gap: clamp(.9rem, 3vw, 2.2rem); }
@@ -163,6 +170,6 @@ body, main, .masthead, .colophon { min-width: 0; }
 }
 @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
   html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
-  .hero-art img, .lab-orbit, .lab-symbol, .lab-progress span, .results.revealed .story-section, .results.revealed .reading-card { animation: none; }
+  .hero-art img, .lab-orbit, .lab-symbol, .lab-bubble, .lab-progress span, .results.revealed .story-section, .results.revealed .reading-card { animation: none; }
   .animal-sticker, .cue-card, .pattern-card, .outlook-card, .primary, .secondary { transition: none; }
 }
